<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan Telecommunication down 3.89 pct.</title>
<headline>Pakistan Telecommunication down 3.89 pct.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Blue chip Pakistan Telecommunication Company Ltd (PTCL) shares dropped 1.15 rupees, or 3.89 percent, to 28.40 on Tuesday after its Global Depositary Receipts (GDR) fell abroad, dealers said.  </p>
<p>More than 6.09 million shares in the company had changed hands on the Karachi bourse by midsession.</p>
<p>&quot;With the change of government, people fear that there will be a further delay in the privatisation of the company,&quot; said chief dealer of Taurus Securities Manochar Jamal. &quot;There is selling of this stock both in international and local markets.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
